      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hello, I think there may be an issue with this line.  It appears that this function is used for opening both files and directories.  However, it is an error to use O_RDWR on a directory.  The open(2) manpage states that doing so will return EISDIR:\n\n    EISDIR pathname refers to a directory and the access requested\n           involved writing (that is, O_WRONLY or O_RDWR is set).\n\n\nI think we should pick the flags based on the mode.  Maybe something like:\n\n    int flags \u003d O_NOATIME;\n    if (S_ISDIR(inode-\u003ei_mode)) {\n      flags |\u003d O_RDONLY;\n    } else {\n      flags |\u003d O_RDWR;\n    }",
      "revId": "c6819dd77861f22858a4371f755c7d5422920eeb",
